phale sakto nibadhyate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1627,\"bb\":1440,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/12/b1440/\",\"shadow_value\":\"yuktaḥ – one who is engaged in devotional service; karma-phalam – the results of all activities; tyaktvā – giving up; śāntim – perfect peace; āpnoti – achieves; naiṣṭhikīm – unflinching; ayuktaḥ – one who is not in Kṛṣṇa consciousness; kāma-kāreṇa – for enjoying the result of work; phale – in the result; saktaḥ – attached; nibadhyate – becomes entangled.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"yuktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who is engaged in devotional service\"},{\"word\":\"karma-phalam\",\"translation\":\"the results of all activities\"},{\"word\":\"tyaktvā\",\"translation\":\"giving up\"},{\"word\":\"śāntim\",\"translation\":\"perfect peace\"},{\"word\":\"āpnoti\",\"translation\":\"achieves\"},{\"word\":\"naiṣṭhikīm\",\"translation\":\"unflinching\"},{\"word\":\"ayuktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who is not in Kṛṣṇa consciousness\"},{\"word\":\"kāma-kāreṇa\",\"translation\":\"for enjoying the result of work\"},{\"word\":\"phale\",\"translation\":\"in the result\"},{\"word\":\"saktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"attached\"},{\"word\":\"nibadhyate\",\"translation\":\"becomes entangled\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1628,\"bb\":1441,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/12/b1441/\",\"body_value\":\"The steadily devoted soul attains unadulterated peace because he offers the result of all activities to Me; whereas a person who is not in union with the Divine, who is greedy for the fruits of his labor, becomes entangled.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1629,\"bb\":1442,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/12/b1